# NOT USED — nihongo has no Caddy of its own.
#
# nihongo is deployed on the same Hetzner host as dmb and abm, and only ONE
# Caddy can bind the host's :80 / :443. That single edge lives in dmb's stack.
# nihongo is served by adding this block to dmb.futari's Caddyfile, alongside
# the existing abm.futari.live block:
#
#   nihongo.futari.live {
#       encode zstd gzip
#       reverse_proxy nihongo-frontend:8080 {
#           # Caddy is the internet-facing edge, so the TCP peer IS the real
#           # client. Overwrite X-Forwarded-For with it, discarding anything the
#           # client sent. Same reasoning as the dmb and abm blocks.
#           header_up X-Forwarded-For {http.request.remote.host}
#       }
#   }
#
# REQUIRES an A record for nihongo.futari.live pointing at this server, and
# dmb's caddy (plus its postgres/redis) attached to the shared external
# `futari` docker network. See DEPLOY.md → "Shared infrastructure".
#
# This file is intentionally inert so no second Caddy is ever started here.
